~ inicial_entering
Jacob: What the hell happened here...?
Jacob: Is that... No, it can’t be.
Jacob steps closer to the body.
Jacob: My son...?
He kneels down, looking closely at the twisted face of the corpse.
Jacob: No... no, they just look similar. He’s even the same age Mike was when he died... Not another one.
Jacob: And what’s going on with his eyes?
He examines the body further.
Jacob: I'm guessing this poor guy is Iggy.
Jacob: I need to contact HQ immediately. They need to bring the other kids in for further interrogations.
Jacob: Also, they should send forensics,I'm sure they can collect some samples from the scene.
He pauses, scanning the room.
Jacob: I should look around. Maybe there’s something important I can use during the interrogations.
Jacob (muttering): God, I hate this job.
=> END

~ collected_cursed_book
Jacob picks up the worn, dust-covered book, its cover etched with unsettling symbols.
Jacob: (thinking) What the hell is this...? Looks like something out of a bad horror movie.
He flips through a few brittle pages, the ink smeared and chaotic, some words crossed out, others circled in red.
Jacob: (grim) Kids playing with this kind of stuff... Did they even know what they were messing with? Or was it just some sick prank that went too far?
He pauses at a page with a strange ritual, a child’s handwriting scrawled in the margins.
Jacob: (quietly) "To summon fear... to wake the dead..." Jesus.
He closes the book slowly, his hands tense.
Jacob: (reflective) Iggy was terrified. They called it a joke... but fear like that doesn’t come from nothing.
He looks around the room, then back at the body.
Jacob: (muttering) And now one of them is dead.
He exhales, jaw clenched.
Jacob: (firmly) This isn’t just a prank gone wrong. Something happened here—and this book might be the key to understanding it.
He tucks the book under his arm.
Jacob: Time to dig deeper.
=> END

~ call_to_HQ
Jacob pulls out his phone, dials HQ, and waits as the line connects.
Jacob: This is Officer Jacob. I’m at the scene now—confirming one deceased, male teenager. Identity unconfirmed, but I believe it's the missing kid, Iggy.
He glances at the body again, then around the room.
Jacob: The body shows signs of trauma... and something’s seriously off with the eyes. Doesn’t look natural.
He tightens his grip on the cursed book under his arm.
Jacob: Found some kind of book—handmade, symbols, rituals... Possibly linked to the victim’s psychological state or group activity. Might’ve been used in a so-called “prank,” but I’m not ruling anything out.
His tone hardens.
Jacob: Get the other kids in—now. I want them all in holding for immediate interrogation. No delays.
He starts heading toward the door.
Jacob: I’m bringing the book back with me. I’ll be at HQ in twenty. Prep the room.
He ends the call without waiting for a reply.
=> END